{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration showed the admission difference. With Advance withheld, the second proposal became an ordinary no-op entry. With early Advance, it remained a configuration entry even though the caller had not applied the first change and the active configuration was unchanged. I’ll fix a check for the Node interface’s local admission guarantee; this history does not demonstrate a consensus safety failure.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cp early_advance_explore_test.go early_advance_check_test.go\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='early_advance_check_test.go';s=open(p).read().replace('TestAssuranceEarlyAdvanceExplore','TestAssuranceEarlyAdvanceAdmission')\ns=s.replace('before:=n.Status()','before:=n.Status()\\\\n  priorApplied:=userApplied>=firstIndex')\ns=s.replace('\\\"first_index\\\":firstIndex,\\\"user_applied\\\":userApplied,\\\"reported_applied\\\":before.Applied','\\\"first_index\\\":firstIndex,\\\"prior_applied_at_proposal\\\":priorApplied,\\\"user_applied\\\":userApplied,\\\"reported_applied\\\":before.Applied')\ns=s.replace('\\\"second_type\\\":secondType.String(),\\\"user_applied\\\"','\\\"second_type\\\":secondType.String(),\\\"prior_applied_at_proposal\\\":priorApplied,\\\"user_applied\\\"')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > build_early_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nclaim='claim-node-conf-admission'\nrefs=['s-node-contract','src-ready-advance','s-leader-admission','n-doc-ready','n-conf-applied','n-node-proposal','s-node-loop','n-status']\nq=dict(question='Does Node preserve its guarantee that a configuration proposal is dropped unless there is no prior unapplied configuration, when its caller uses the documented early Advance optimization and defers ApplyConfChange in application order?',importance='Allowing a later configuration entry while the prior configuration is inactive bypasses the stated membership-serialization protection. The local admission defect may affect quorum-change safety, but the selected learner-only history measures no safety failure.',source_ids=list(refs),participants=['Node leader','caller persisting Ready','caller applying committed configuration'],objects=['f-membership active configuration','pendingConfIndex','raftLog.applied','first committed configuration entry','second configuration proposal'],contexts=['Synchronous Node API with early Advance permitted by Node documentation','First configuration persisted and committed but not yet applied through ApplyConfChange','Applications remain ordered; second proposal arrives before first application'],event_paths=['First committed configuration Ready -> persist -> Advance before application -> second ProposeConfChange -> inspect actual emitted Entry type -> finish applying both entries in order'],activity_classes=['A1','A4','A5'],behavior_ids=['b-configuration','b-replication','b-application'],fact_ids=['f-membership'],supporting_behavior_ids={'b-api':'Node exposes both early Advance and configuration admission contract, serializing actual calls.','b-persistence':'Advance supplies internal application completion bookkeeping independently of delayed external ApplyConfChange.'},obligation_relation_kind='consumption',counterevidence=['Withholding Advance retains the guard and rewrites the second proposal to EntryNormal.','RawNode.Advance comment describes completed application; the history uses Node, whose interface and package documentation explicitly permit early Advance.','Applying the first change before Advance admits the second legitimately.','Ordinary state-machine completion can lag internal Applied under the documented optimization; the question concerns the separate ApplyConfChange-dependent active configuration.'],unknowns=['Whether documentation intended an unstated exception requiring ApplyConfChange before early Advance; no such exception was found in the captured Node or package interface.','Global safety consequences are not established by a single-voter learner-only history.'],trigger_rationale='Exploration 66fd200abfdc4ed7b01245892d2e04b4 reached public Node calls with actual commitment: early Advance makes internal Applied=3 while caller Applied=2 and learners remain zero, and the second entry is EntryConfChange. Hold-Advance control produces EntryNormal. This directly discriminates the stated admission duty without constructing a safety history from disputed generic protocol expectations.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='direct_test')\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids']:q['source_ids']+=b['source_ids']\nfor f in m['facts']:\n if f['id'] in q['fact_ids']:q['source_ids']+=f['source_ids']\nq['source_ids']=sorted(set(q['source_ids']))\nbs=[]\nfor id,mat,sym,a,b,desc in [('bind-node-conf-admission','s-leader-admission','stepLeader',1267,1345,'Configuration proposal checks pendingConfIndex against raftLog.applied.'),('bind-node-early-advance','src-ready-advance','Advance',477,494,'RawNode Advance consumes deferred application completion generated by accepted Ready; Node delegates to it.')]:\n bs.append(dict(id=id,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['s-node-contract','n-doc-ready','n-conf-applied'],rationale='Node.ProposeConfChange promises rejection while a prior configuration remains unapplied; Node.Advance and package instructions permit advancing before application completes, while configuration becomes active only through application.')]))\nbids=[b['id'] for b in bs]\ng=dict(source_ids=refs,expectation_ids=['s-node-contract','n-doc-ready','n-conf-applied'],binding_ids=bids,derivation='Node.ProposeConfChange states changes are dropped unless the leader is certain no prior unapplied configuration remains. Node.Advance explicitly permits overlap with application; doc.go permits any time after persistence, preserving application order. Configuration active membership changes at application. A caller-compliant early Advance therefore must not substitute for applying the configuration when admitting another change. This is local entry eligibility, not an inferred consensus safety theorem.',applicability='Node API, synchronous Ready/Advance, prior committed config not rejected by caller and deferred ApplyConfChange, ordered eventual application.',unresolved=['An unstated configuration-specific exception to early Advance would change applicability; it is not present in the captured Node/package contract.'],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Interpreting all Advance calls as completed application contradicts the Node-specific early-Advance permission, although that stronger description occurs on RawNode.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='For callers complying with Node Ready/Advance ordering, a second proposed configuration change must not be appended as a configuration entry while an earlier committed configuration change has not yet been applied through ApplyConfChange (and has not been rejected by the application). The documented early Advance optimization does not itself apply the earlier configuration.',source_ids=refs,scope=dict(description='Node-level configuration-proposal admission under documented early Advance, with persisted committed first change, delayed but ordered ApplyConfChange, and configuration validation enabled.',assumptions=['Node interface early Advance permission applies to a Ready containing configuration entries; no captured exception restricts it to data entries.','Prior configuration is intended to apply, not cancelled.','Target runs serialized Node loop; caller uses no direct state mutations.'],excluded=['RawNode callers interpreting Advance as completed application.','Consensus safety failure, voter-set replacement, crash recovery and client completion.','Configurations proposed with DisableConfChangeValidation enabled.']),pending=[],grounding=g)\ncand=dict(action='obligation',rationale='Fix the explicit local Node admission responsibility from the captured interface, preserving the stronger RawNode wording as a boundary and no global consequence claim.',question=q,obligation=ob,bindings=bs)\nleg=dict(g);leg['derivation']='Public RestartNode starts a single voter from snapshot index/term 1 and matching HardState/Applied. Campaign and Ready/Advance create actual leader commitment. Persist all entries and HardState, preserve application order, and defer only first ApplyConfChange under Node early-Advance permission. Propose the second via public Node, use Status as a serialization fence, inspect emitted entries, then finish application in original order. The hold and apply-first controls vary only the Advance/application placement. Messages to unavailable learners may be dropped; no peer vote or acknowledgment is forged.'\nplan=dict(description='Fix the explored Node configuration-admission comparison in three histories: hold_advance, early_advance, apply_then_advance. For each actual first configuration committed at first_index, record caller application state immediately before second proposal, observe the second appended entry type, and then finish all application duties. Compare only the required implication: if first was unapplied at proposal, the second must not remain EntryConfChange. Apply-first is a permitted-path diagnostic without a mandatory acceptance oracle.',claim_id=claim,binding_ids=bids,harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Actual Node goroutine and public API, one initial voter and sequential learner additions, synchronous MemoryStorage persistence. Context timeout and bounded Ready loops fail prerequisites rather than report protocol violations.',semantic_changes=['No target changes; MemoryStorage substitutes completed durability and absent learners receive no network messages.','Separate userApplied counter advances only after caller application/ApplyConfChange; Status.Applied is recorded independently.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='proposal',event='before_second',conditions=[])],legality=leg),monitors=[dict(id='monitor-node-conf-admission',checker_id='node-conf-admission',event='second_appended',binding_ids=bids,admission_alias='proposal',applicability_conditions=[],grounding=dict(g,derivation='Admission event records actual prior caller application before the second public proposal; result retains that captured value and the actual appended Entry.Type. Identity scenario+first_index correlates each independent history. The implication only forbids a configuration entry when prior_applied_at_proposal is false. Held-Advance result may be emitted after caller later applies the first change, so current user_applied is not substituted for admission-time state. No result filtering by expected type occurs.'))],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='node-conf-admission',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='event',op='eq',value='second_appended'),antecedent=dict(field='prior_applied_at_proposal',op='eq',value=False),assertion=dict(field='second_type',op='ne',value='EntryConfChange'),identity_fields=['scenario','first_index'],description='When the preceding committed configuration was still unapplied at second-proposal admission, the second proposal must be dropped/replaced rather than retained as an EntryConfChange.')],uncertainties=['The applicability interpretation uses explicit Node early-Advance permission; RawNode completion wording is stronger and not used to authorize the history.','Only local admission of learner changes is measured; safety or availability consequences require a different legal history.'])\nopen('early_plan.json','w').write(json.dumps(plan,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\ns=dict(action='check',rationale='Create the local Node admission obligation and fix a fresh direct check using the actual API and three ordering controls. Exploration is construction knowledge only.',candidate=cand,plan_path='early_plan.json',harness_path='early_advance_check_test.go',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['66fd200abfdc4ed7b01245892d2e04b4']+refs,answered='The Node exploration completed all three histories. With Advance withheld, second index 4 is EntryNormal. Early Advance reports Applied=3 while userApplied=2 and no learners are active, then appends second index 4 as EntryConfChange before first ApplyConfChange. Apply-first control also appends EntryConfChange, with first application already complete. All histories subsequently complete ordered application. This is an exploratory admission difference; no global safety result follows.',remaining=['Run the fixed check and review the Node contract interpretation, operation correlation and actual timing before attribution.'],rationale='Explicit Node interface wording grounds the local obligation; tests compare actual entry classification with independently tracked caller application at proposal time.'))\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython3 build_early_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
